  "features": [
    "Bounded, rebased connection/stream flow credit with retained negative debt after stream settings reductions.",
    "Connection window API remains separate from stream initial-window settings.",
    "FIFO settings snapshots and per-update callbacks, with pending-state tracking and explicit cancellation.",
    "Encoded/retained custom settings and requested peer identifiers, using actual numeric JavaScript properties.",
    "Acknowledged receive limits retain valid in-flight allowances; graceful close waits for outstanding settings work."
  ],
  "verification_scope": "Valid protocol conformance and source-level defensive bounds. No adversarial wire reproduction was performed. Original assertions, fixtures, allocations and case deadlines are unchanged.",
  "limitations": [
    "Initial valid conformance passed eight of nine files; custom settings and ordered callback/lifetime failures were retained. Superseded generated output with an unknown cancellation intrinsic was not credited as final verification.",
    "Disk-guard refusals and cache cleanups are retained without test credit. Cleanup removed only verified duplicate evidence or obsolete cache outputs after terminal builds, preserving current source/executable outputs.",
    "This is a nine-file conformance checkpoint, not proof that the previous 893-entry or complete Bun suite passes. Remaining internal HTTP2/Undici, wire/state, TLS, conflicting assertions (#868), whole-suite and Release/ASAN/all-platform scope remain open under #66/#867."
  ],
